{{!-- The numbers, in one line: the COLLAPSED density of the top band.

      One component, two densities — the steading's own device. This is not a second, compact copy
      of the numbers; it is the same numbers at line height, and the fold handle picks between them.
      Both densities are in the markup at every width, and this one stands down while the band is on
      screen.

      The six stats, in the pairs the conditions hinder, each pair followed by its condition. HP,
      Armor and Damage are the rail's (D7) and are not repeated here. The three pairs are contiguous
      in the canonical order and cover all six exactly once, which is what makes this drawable; the
      grouping comes from the snapshot (StatPairSnapshot).

      Plain readouts, not tiles: at line height there is no size at which the woodcut frame is a
      frame rather than a smudge. The name is still the roll button, exactly as at full density —
      a stat you cannot roll from the line makes the fold cost the thing it was for. It does NOT
      borrow the tile's `.stonetop-stat-roll` class: that one is absolutely positioned on the frame's
      rule. Every value is named for assistive tech, so nothing here is a bare number.

      Context: the root. --}}
<div class="stonetop-folded-ledger" aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.foldedLedger'}}">
	<ul class="stonetop-folded-pairs stonetop-unmarked">
		{{#each stonetop.statPairs}}
		<li class="stonetop-folded-pair{{#if debility.active}} is-active{{/if}}">
			<ul class="stonetop-folded-stats stonetop-unmarked">
				{{#each stats}}
				<li class="stonetop-folded-stat{{#if ../debility.active}} is-hindered{{/if}}" data-stat="{{key}}">
					<button type="button" class="stonetop-folded-abbr rollable" data-roll="{{key}}"
					        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.rollStatNamed' stat=name}}"
					        data-tooltip="{{description}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP">{{abbr}}</button>
					<span class="stonetop-folded-value">{{value}}</span>
					{{!-- The hindered ones say why, rather than only looking different: color is never the
					      only carrier of anything. --}}
					<span class="stonetop-folded-sr">{{#if ../debility.active}}{{../debility.name}}{{/if}}</span>
				</li>
				{{/each}}
			</ul>
			{{!-- The condition, on the pair it hinders: which stats one touches has to be knowable BEFORE
			      it is marked, since marking one is often a choice between them. A real control — this
			      is the density on screen during play, when conditions are marked — through the same
			      `debility` change action as the bracket. --}}
			<label class="stonetop-folded-cond" data-tooltip="{{debility.description}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP">
				<input type="checkbox" class="stonetop-cond-check" data-change-action="debility" data-slug="{{debility.key}}"
				       {{#if debility.active}}checked{{/if}} {{#unless @root.editable}}disabled{{/unless}}>
				<span class="stonetop-cond-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<span class="stonetop-folded-cond-name">{{debility.name}}</span>
				<span class="stonetop-visually-hidden">{{debility.description}}</span>
			</label>
		</li>
		{{/each}}
	</ul>
</div>
